WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.680
APFS is Apple's modern file system used on many macOS systems.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:13.300
At a high level, analysts care about how file metadata, timestamps, snapshots, permissions, ownership, and volume structure affect evidence.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:18.480
File timestamps can support timeline reconstruction, but they need careful interpretation.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:25.020
Normal application behavior, sync tools, updates, and investigator actions can all change metadata.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:30.200
Permissions and ownership help explain which users or processes could access files.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:37.140
Hidden files and dot directories can contain shell configuration, application state, developer artifacts, and user settings.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:46.800
Downloads and execution clues may appear in file metadata, quarantine attributes, browser artifacts, application logs, and endpoint telemetry.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:51.180
The strongest analysis compares several sources rather than relying on one marker.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:57.000
Quarantine attributes can help indicate that a file may have been downloaded or received from an external source.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:03.460
They are useful clues, but they do not automatically prove maliciousness, user intent, or execution.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.960
A file can have a quarantine attribute and be harmless.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:09.180
A suspicious file may lack one.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:18.200
Analysts should interpret quarantine data alongside downloads, browser history, logs, timestamps, signatures, and user activity.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.580
Timelines connect the investigation.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:33.520
A useful macOS timeline may combine file metadata, unified logs, application artifacts, plists, launch item changes, browser records, endpoint telemetry, and cloud or identity events.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:38.860
The analyst should note time zones, clock issues, collection limitations, and uncertainty.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:43.480
A timeline should make the evidence easier to reason about, not hide weak assumptions.
